}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":20,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I made the table-lookup change, but the acceptance command could not run as written, and the change itself is not committed anywhere. The target file is in the read-only `external/sdkjs` clone, so the change only exists there and as a patch pasted into the packet's Executor log.\n\n**What changed** (`external/sdkjs/common/libfont/common.js`)\n- The original switch is kept as a reference function, `hb_get_script_horizontal_direction_switch`, also exported on `AscFonts`.\n- At load, that switch is run once over every `AscFonts.HB_SCRIPT` value. The scripts that are not left-to-right go into a `Map`, so the table gives the same answer as the switch by construction.\n- The public function returns left-to-right straight away for Latin and Common, otherwise looks up the `Map`, and returns left-to-right by default.\n\n**Checks**\n- **Same results:** I compared table and switch over all 166 script values plus odd inputs (0, -1, 2³²−1, `undefined`, `null`): no differences.\n- **Speed:** timed in Node with 408k calls, mostly Latin and Common:\n\n  | V8 mode | switch | table |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | fully optimised | 2.94 ms | 2.06 ms |\n  | `--no-opt` | 134 ms | 13.2 ms |\n  | `--jitless` | 118 ms | 23.4 ms |\n\n  The 43 ms seen in the browser profile from PKT-0072 matches the non-optimised rows, so the expected gain there is about 30–40 ms. That estimate is not measured in the browser.\n- **Tests:** `.theseus/oracle/sdkjs-common.sh` passes 6/6 suites (the known-broken ones as already recorded).\n\n**Decisions**\n- **A `Map`, not an array:** script ids are 32-bit HarfBuzz tags, not small indices.\n- **The Latin/Common shortcut was added after measuring:** a plain `Map` lookup was slower than the switch once V8 fully optimises (4.7 vs 3.0 ms).\n\n**Not done**\n- **Acceptance command:** `.theseus/oracle/perf/profile-fonts.js` is not on this branch; it is only on `pkt/PKT-0072` (commit 75204fd). `<samples-dir>` is a placeholder. The script also profiles the installed Document Server bundle, which a source change does not touch without a rebuild and a mirror of the install.\n- **Unit test:** the packet's goal asks for one, but `create_in` is empty, so I could not create a test file.\n- **Follow-up:** I recorded a request in `.theseus/spawn/` to land the change through an sdkjs fork, add the unit test, and measure it in the browser. Its target, contract and acceptance are filled in.\n\nThe packet log, the friction line and the spawn request are committed as `11c4055`; `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 1 warning.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- Check a micro-optimisation in both fully optimised and `--no-opt` V8: a bare `Map` lookup can lose to an optimised switch.\n- Packets that target `external/` cannot deliver code until an sdkjs fork exists.\n- Acceptance commands should name scripts that exist on the base branch.","ttft_ms":2640,"type":"result","duration_ms":260326,"uuid":"14991be2-d46d-4146-afd5-ead7f985a192","ttft_stream_ms":1664,"time_to_request_ms":970,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":13,"system_prompt":427,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":15,"input_attachments":70,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":11,"transcript_persist":56,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":17,"engine_pickup":34,"loop_entry":27,"message_prep":8,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":33,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":27,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":189,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":18},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":642,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":238,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":213,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":229,"process_anon_mib_result":136,"process_peak_rss_mib":247,"process_cpu_ms_turn":5647,"process_wall_ms_turn":260325,"process_cp